WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.620
Varys: Though House Durrandon titled themselves
"Storm Kings," they were little more than

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.620
gusts.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.960
Their kingdom in the Stormlands had been doddering
to its end for the past few centuries, helped

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.010
along by other houses.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.119
Most of all by House Hoare, who were nearly
finished with a monstrous castle at Harrenhal,

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:22.750
too large and too costly a seat to rule only
the Riverlands.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.820
King Argilac knew where the Ironborn would
soon turn.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.920
You'd think a king who wanted to keep his
crown would be wary of a man with fire-breathing

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.370
monsters, but King ArgilacDurrandon wasn't
called "the Arrogant" for nothing.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:42.450
Determined to arrest decline, he sent an envoy
to Dragonstone to enlist Aegon Targaryen and

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.540
his dragons against his enemies.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:50.260
In exchange, Argilac offered lands he didn't
have, and a wife Aegon didn't need.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:56.310
For as the Valyrians did, Aegon had wed his
elder sister Visenya.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:01:00.730
Then as the Valyrians didn't, he took the
younger Rhaenys as well.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.610
Two sisters, two wives.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.530
Perhaps that's why he was so keen to get off
Dragonstone.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.830
Aegon countered Argilac with courtesy.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:15.610
He sent his own envoy requesting that Princess
Durrandon's hand be given instead to Aegon's

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:20.560
closest friend and rumored half-brother, Orys
Baratheon.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.890
Argilac answered with a box and a note: "These
are the only hands your bastard shall have

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:26.890
of me."

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.350
Inside the box were the hands of Aegon's envoy.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.900
How long had Aegon been waiting for such a
pretext?

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:40.990
As his army prepared to sail, ravens flew
to every great lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:47.120
All bore the same message: From this day forth,
there would be but one king in Westeros.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.530
Those who bent the knee to Aegon of House
Targaryen would keep their lands and titles.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:57.549
Those who took up arms against him would be
thrown down, humbled and destroyed.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:00.150
Poor old Argilac.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.320
He couldn't even match Aegon in arrogance.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:08.289
Varys: While Aegon marched on Harrenhal after
his coronation, Orys Baratheon had taken most

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:13.080
of his forces, and his queen Rhaenys with
her dragon, south to deal with the excuse

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:18.470
for the invasion: Argilac the Arrogant, King
of the Stormlands.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:23.460
Argilac had his seat at Storm's End, a castle
considered the most impregnable in Westeros

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.380
after Harrenhal.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.440
Argilac may have been arrogant, but he wasn't
stupid or a coward.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.741
His lords advised him to shut his gates and
wait out the siege, but he'd heard what had

00:02:34.741 --> 00:02:40.450
happened at Harrenhal and refused to die a
suckling pig cooked in his own castle.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:45.950
He would meet victory or defeat the same way,
with sword in hand.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.900
He called his banners and marched to meet
Orys Baratheon in the field.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:57.069
Thanks to Rhaenys' dragon, Meraxes, Orys knew
Argilac was coming, how many men he had, and

00:02:57.069 --> 00:02:58.970
how fast he marched.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:04.740
So Orys simply seized the high ground and
dug in on the hills to wait for Argilac.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.250
As the two armies approached, the wind rose
to meet them, and the rain poured from the

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:14.739
sky, a gale which would give the battle its
name: the Last Storm.

00:03:14.739 --> 00:03:20.770
King Argilac's lords urged him to wait for
the weather to die down, but the Storm King

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:26.379
saw that the rain was blowing into the faces
of the Baratheon men on their hills and Argilac

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:32.430
outnumbered the Baratheon host two to one,
with four times as many knights and heavy

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.440
horse.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.519
Argilac attacked.

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:41.990
Three times Argilac led his knights against
the Baratheon line, but the hills were steep,

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.129
and the rain had beat the earth mud.

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:49.700
The warhorses foundered and slipped, and the
chargers collapsed.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.849
The battle seemed lost until Argilac ordered
the spearmen up the hill.

00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:58.950
Blinded by the rain, the Baratheons didn't
see them until it was too late.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:06.940
One hill fell, then another and another until
only one remained in the Baratheon center.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:13.200
If Argilac could break through there, he could
split the invading army and flank both halves.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:21.080
Argilac and his men charged, and the Baratheon
line broke, revealing Queen Rhaenys and Meraxes.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:25.560
Argilac's vanguard burst into flame, and his
men panicked.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:30.460
The victory charge fell into chaos, and Argilac
himself was thrown from his horse.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.060
But he didn't yield.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:38.500
When Orys Baratheon arrived, he found the
old king holding off half-a-dozen men, another

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.389
half-dozen dead at his feet.

00:04:41.389 --> 00:04:46.530
Orys dismounted to meet the king on equal
footing and offered Argilac one final chance

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.330
to yield.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.800
Argilac cursed him instead.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:55.960
As the storm raged around them, the grizzled
old warrior and the bearded upstart fought

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.889
for life and kingdom.

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:01.870
In the end, Argilac got his wish.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.530
He died, sword in hand.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:11.960
As word of Argilac's death spread, his lords
and knights threw down their swords and fled.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:17.110
Orys and his vanguard rode to Storm's End
to claim Argilac's castle for Aegon, only

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.030
to find the gates barred and the walls manned.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:26.180
Argilac's daughter had assumed his crown,
and the new Storm Queen was as fond of yielding

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.940
as her father.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:32.660
She declared that Orys would win only bones,
blood, and ashes here.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:39.470
But her men were weaker than her, and that
night Orys found Argilac's daughter delivered,

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:43.030
gagged, chained, and naked to his camp.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.880
Argilac had refused to give Orys her hand.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.840
Now, Orys could have any part of her he wished.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:55.539
But Orys unchained the girl, wrapped his cloak
around her, and poured her a glass of wine.

00:05:55.539 --> 00:06:00.050
He told her he would take the arms, banner,
and words of House Durrandon to honor her

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:02.910
father's courage in the Last Storm.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:06.780
Conveniently, Orys had none of his own to
discard first.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:12.780
The crowned stag became the sigil of House
Baratheon, and Storm's End their seat.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:17.522
Argilac's daughter would even remain in her
home, though, as a lady instead of a princess.

00:06:17.522 --> 00:06:25.320
The Stormlands were now Aegon's, and as tribute,
Aegon demanded the swords of the men Orys

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.970
had defeated.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:29.970
For what purpose, Orys didn't know.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:35.850
Stannis Baratheon: My brother, Robert Baratheon,
had raised the banners of Storm's End, our

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.830
ancestral castle, against the Mad King Aerys.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:45.430
Jon Arryn of the Vale and Eddard Stark of
the North stood with him, and Hoster Tully

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.510
of the Riverlands would join.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:53.901
But their lands were far from ours and separated
by the combined strength of the West, the

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:57.919
Reach, and King's Landing itself.

00:06:57.919 --> 00:07:00.069
Even Robert's own lords were against him.

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:07.169
It was the hardest choice I've ever made:
my brother or my king, blood or honor.

00:07:07.169 --> 00:07:11.370
Aerys ruled by right of all the laws in Westeros.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.490
Everyone knew the price of defiance.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:19.860
But there are deeper, older laws: the younger
brother bows before the elder.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.240
I followed Robert.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:28.810
Early in the war, Mace Tyrell's indecisive
victory at Ashford cut Robert off from Storm's

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:29.810
End.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:36.520
Instead of pursuing Robert, and risking his
record, Mace Tyrell turned east and laid siege

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.420
to our home.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:44.290
His vast army and navy encircled us and preventing
any resupply by land or sea.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.160
If a wagon tried to reach us, it was burned.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.990
If a ship tried to land, it was sunk.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.139
We were locked inside Storm's End to starve.

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:56.840
But Robert had commanded me to hold the castle
no matter the cost.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:01.919
He could ill afford to lose his ancient seat,
which had never fallen.

00:08:01.919 --> 00:08:08.960
While Robert smashed Rhaegar on the Trident,
my men ate the dogs because the horses had

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.240
already been devoured.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:16.039
While the Lannisters sacked King's Landing,
we ate the rats.

00:08:16.039 --> 00:08:21.060
If the smuggler Davos had not slipped through
the Tyrell blockade with his onions, we'd

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.259
have eaten our own dead.

00:08:24.259 --> 00:08:31.580
But I held the castle until Lord Eddard remembered
us, and marched to lift the siege.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:39.189
The Tyrells didn't even put up a fight, and
Robert threw a feast to celebrate Lord Eddard's

00:08:39.189 --> 00:08:40.479
"victory."

00:08:40.479 --> 00:08:45.449
I was sent to the royal island stronghold
of Dragonstone to deal with Viserys and Daenerys,

00:08:45.449 --> 00:08:48.550
the last surviving Targaryen children.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:54.709
Before I arrived, however, they had escaped
across the Narrow Sea.

00:08:54.709 --> 00:08:56.029
Robert was furious.

00:08:56.029 --> 00:09:06.180
He stripped me of Storm's End and gave it
to that prancing fool Renly, my younger brother.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:08.939
I could keep Dragonstone.

00:09:08.939 --> 00:09:12.790
The Baratheons say, "Ours is the Fury."

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:16.069
I will show them fury burns.

00:09:16.069 --> 00:09:23.209
Robert Baratheon: For our rebellion to succeed,
King's Landing had to be taken, forcefully.

00:09:23.209 --> 00:09:29.879
No one was foolish enough to believe that
Aerys was gonna hand his crown over peacefully.

00:09:29.879 --> 00:09:34.250
The Mad King's reign needed to end.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:40.369
What Tywin Lannister's forces did was unfortunate,
but it was necessary to secure the Iron Throne,

00:09:40.369 --> 00:09:44.519
and bring peace and justice to the Seven Kingdoms.

00:09:44.519 --> 00:09:50.370
My glorious victory at the Trident left me
wounded, but I sent my personal maester to

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:55.899
attend to Ser Barristan Selmy instead; his
wounds were more severe.

00:09:55.899 --> 00:10:00.559
Even though Ser Barristan was a member of
Aerys's Kingsguard and fought on the opposing

00:10:00.559 --> 00:10:05.209
side, that man's bravery and loyalty were
something to behold.

00:10:05.209 --> 00:10:10.370
But this meant my wounds would take longer
to heal and I couldn't ride to King's Landing

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:11.660
myself.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:18.320
I sent the one man I trusted over anyone else
in this world, Ned Stark, in my place.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:23.040
Had I been able to ride, perhaps I could have
reached King's Landing sooner and prevented

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.449
some of the violence that occurred when the
Lannisters entered the city.

00:10:27.449 --> 00:10:32.360
Still, what Lord Tywin did was for the greater
good.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:36.089
Even what happened to Princess Elia and her
children.

00:10:36.089 --> 00:10:43.360
Babies or no, theirs was the same cursed blood
that flowed within the Mad King's veins.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:47.620
They were dragonspawn and couldn't be allowed
to survive.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.519
What would they grow to be?

00:10:50.519 --> 00:10:52.139
Loyal subjects?

00:10:52.139 --> 00:10:56.200
Ned, with his damn northern honor.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:03.350
He and I had our first major fight over the
deaths of the Targaryen children.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:06.110
Ned called it murder.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.110
Murder!?

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:10.709
It was war!...

00:11:10.709 --> 00:11:13.959
It was war...

00:11:13.959 --> 00:11:18.279
Lord Stark demanded that the Lannisters be
held responsible for their crimes.

00:11:18.279 --> 00:11:22.579
Was it a crime to put an end to a family of
lunatics born of incest?

00:11:22.579 --> 00:11:25.990
I wouldn't - and still won't - blame Tywin.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:31.249
Instead, I sent Ned Stark south to finish
off the remaining Targaryen loyalists.

